@startuml test-e2e-topology
!include style.iuml

title Container end-to-end and contract topology (L4, L5)

node "CI runner or developer machine" {
  node "pytest runner\ncaldav library, requests" as runner
  folder "certs\nthrowaway CA, test only" as certs
  node "Docker compose network" {
    node "bridge :5232\nimage from Dockerfile" as bridge
    node "bridge-labels :5233\nsame image, GroupByLabel" as labels
    node "donetick-stub :9091\ndotnet-wiremock 2.19.0,\nsame mappings as L2" as stub
    node "donetick :2021\nrelease binary v0.1.82,\nSQLite" as real
    node "bridge-contract :5234\nsame image" as cbridge
  }
}

runner --> bridge : CalDAV over HTTPS\n(Basic auth)
runner --> labels : CalDAV over HTTPS
bridge --> stub : eAPI
labels --> stub : eAPI
runner ..> stub : admin API:\nverify requests
runner ..> real : provision user and token,\nseed, contract checks
runner ..> cbridge : CalDAV over HTTPS
cbridge ..> real : eAPI
bridge ..> certs : mounted read-only

note right of real
  Profile contract. The runner provisions
  a user and an API token over the REST
  API, then starts bridge-contract with it.
end note

note bottom of runner
  Also checks container behaviour: restart keeps
  ETags, invalid configuration exits non-zero,
  stub outage gives 502 and the service recovers.
end note
@enduml
